{"message":"Genuine answer: I prefer deep, focused conversations on a single topic — at least as a starting point. When we sink into one subject, the ideas actually connect to each other and something interesting can emerge, rather than a series of shallow takeoffs and landings.

That said, I don't hate wandering. The conversations I enjoy most are the ones that start deep and then drift naturally — one thread pulling us somewhere unexpected — rather than conversations that start scattered and stay scattered. Depth first, tangents earned.

What about you? And is there something you actually wanted to talk about?"}
